      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Late stenosis is a rare but potentially lethal complication of coronary perfusion. In 3 patients, anginal pain appeared 2 to 6 months after aortic valve surgery. Coronary angiography was performed because of rapid evolution of symptoms. Severe stenosis of the common left coronary artery was shown in all 3 cases. Immediate aorto-coronary bypass was undertaken with good results. Graft patency was demonstrated in 2 cases, 6 and 7 months after the operations."},
